## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q1: Stock enforcement strictness** — Should the POS **hard-block** selling when stock is insufficient (zero or negative)? Or should it allow overselling with a warning? Current system has no stock checks at all. I will implement **hard-block on backend** (reject checkout if stock < requested quantity for non-custom items) with a clear error message, but allow managers/admins to override. Please confirm.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q2: Credit sales flow** — The system has `CustomerService::addCreditSale()` which updates customer balance. When payment method is "credit", should the sale still record a safe transaction? Currently sales always create a safe transaction. For credit sales, I'll skip the safe transaction (since no cash exchanged) and only update the customer's balance. Please confirm.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q3: Layout preference** — Should the POS use a **split layout** (product grid on left, cart on right — like most modern POS systems)? Or keep the current **full-width cart** with the product grid above it? I recommend the split layout for a professional POS experience.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q4: Shift requirement** — Should the POS **require** an open shift before allowing sales? The system has shift management but POS currently doesn't check. I'll add a check that warns if no shift is open, but still allows sales. Please confirm.

